{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Asymptotics"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.not_infinitesimal_and_not_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.not_infinitesimal_and_not_finite","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L173-L184","doc":"**The two parts are about the same value at most one way.**\n\nA non-zero value cannot be both infinitesimal and non-finite: parts 1 and 3\nwould put its leading exponent strictly below and strictly above `0`. Exercises\nboth fields together, and is the statement that the conjecture is internally\ncoherent rather than describing two unrelated regimes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.Ow_normalises_on_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.Ow_normalises_on_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L150-L171","doc":"**The class pins `Ow` on the embedded reals** — anti-vacuity.\n\nFor non-zero `r : ℝ`, both fields fire and force `Ow (ofReal r) = 0` exactly.\n`OmegaOrder` alone cannot give this: `Ow_ofReal_mul` says rescaling by a\nnon-zero real leaves the leading exponent unchanged, which constrains\ndifferences and never fixes an absolute value.\n\nSo the two fields are not inert decoration — they have a consequence that\nconstrains `Ow` on a set the caller does not choose, and an instance cannot be\nmanufactured by adjusting `Ow` freely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.not_finite_iff_Ow_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.not_finite_iff_Ow_pos","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L128-L128","doc":"**Part 3 — singularity formation.** A non-zero value fails to be finite\nexactly when its leading exponent is positive. Applied to an eigenvalue,\nthis is \"a divergence has `Ow(λ) > 0`\", and the exponent is what\nclassifies the divergence type.\n\nThe hypothesis `x ≠ 0` is load-bearing for the same reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.infinitesimal_iff_Ow_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.infinitesimal_iff_Ow_neg","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L120-L120","doc":"**Part 1 — gap closure.** A non-zero value is infinitesimal exactly when\nits leading exponent is negative. Applied to `Δ = λ₂ − λ₁`, this is\n\"the gap closes in the classical limit iff `Ow(Δ) < 0`\".\n\nThe hypothesis `x ≠ 0` is load-bearing: `0` is infinitesimal but has\n`Ow 0 = ⊤`, so the biconditional is false there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SpectralNormalForm","kind":"class","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SpectralNormalForm.lean#L100-L129","doc":"**Spectral normal form**: the surreal order and the ω-adic valuation agree\nabout smallness and largeness.\n\nThe conjecture of\n[`conj:spectral-normal-form`](../../../appendix-surreals/spectral-normal-form.md),\nwhich is what lets spectral gap closure and singularity formation as `q → 1` be\nread directly off leading exponents, with no analytic limit.\n\n`K` is the caller's surreal carrier together with its ω-adic order. An instance\n**is** the conjecture, for that carrier. None is provided — and see the header:\nno `OmegaOrder` instance exists anywhere in this tree, so the class has not been\nexhibited satisfiable either. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:spectral-normal-form","label":"conj:spectral-normal-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/spectral-normal-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}